    "content": "Former U.S. President Barack Obama has publicly condemned the investigation into Congresswoman Ilhan Omar by the administration of President Donald Trump, describing it as an improper use of government authority against a vocal critic. Obama said the probe appears to target Omar for her political views and statements, which he argued undermines a core democratic principle.\n\nThe investigation into Omar, a Minnesota Democrat and one of the first Muslim women elected to Congress, has drawn attention amid ongoing political tensions. Obama's remarks come as the Trump administration faces scrutiny over the handling of inquiries into political opponents. Obama, who has largely stayed out of day-to-day political disputes since leaving office, used his statement to emphasize that democracy requires protecting citizens from government retaliation based on speech or political beliefs.\n\nObama argued that the actions against Omar endanger that fundamental principle and should concern all Americans, regardless of party affiliation. He called on the public to pay attention to the case and to defend the right to political expression. The former president did not specify what steps, if any, he believes should be taken, but his comments add a high-profile voice to the debate over the investigation.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, the case is particularly significant. Omar, who was born in Somalia and immigrated to the United States as a child, has been a prominent voice for immigrant communities and a frequent target of political attacks. Her treatment by federal authorities is closely watched by Somali Americans, who see it as a test of whether their community's representatives can operate without fear of retribution. Obama's defense of Omar may resonate with diaspora members who view her as a symbol of political empowerment.\n\nThe controversy also highlights broader questions about the use of government power and the protection of minority voices in U.S. politics. As the investigation continues, its outcome could set a precedent for how elected officials from immigrant backgrounds are treated. Obama's intervention suggests the issue will remain in the national spotlight.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/10/19/obama-oo-ka-digay-beegsiga-siyaasadeed-ee-ilhaan-cumar/",
